<Scene>
<WorldInfo title='Brain Loom hero scene' info='"title: Brain Loom hero scene - glass cortex, wet cortex, golden deep structures" "sources: cortex = TemplateFlow tpl-fsaverage 10k pial, Desikan-Killiany labels, sulc (FreeSurfer lineage, Fischl et al. 1999; licence grade Suspected, no licence file found). Geometry is the template&apos;s own 10,242 vertex set per hemisphere (a lower-resolution version of the 164k surface that TemplateFlow distributes; NOT decimated by us), moved rigidly (axes reordered, origin at the pial bounding-box centre) and re-encoded to 0.1 mm with the medial-wall triangles dropped; the cortex itself is not scaled (1.000)" "sources: deep structures = marching cubes on tpl-MNI152NLin2009cAsym 1 mm aseg, T1 slices = same template brain T1w (Fonov 2009 and 2011; permissive MNI licence text, copyright notice retained; grade Confirmed)" "ALIGNMENT NOTICE: the deep structures and the T1 slices come from MNI152NLin2009cAsym and are carried into the fsaverage cortex frame by a per-axis scale and shift that makes the two cortex bounding boxes equal (scale .963 .966 .952, shift mm .5 -1.3 1.1; RAS x y z). It is a look-level fit, NOT a registration." "SYNTHETIC NOTICE: the 497 tract arcs (13916 points) are generated between Desikan region vertices and are not tractography of any subject or scan. Activation blobs are ILLUSTRATIVE, not measured activity." "AO: Cycles per-vertex AO bake (bake_out_10k.npz), matches mesh vertex for vertex" "slice window: T1 intensity 3250.0 to 9369.0 (p2 to p99.7 of non-zero voxels), gamma 0.85, alpha smoothstep(0.07,0.42)*0.9; of the tissue voxels on the six slices 0.31% clip at the top, 5.04% clip at the bottom (drawn as the darkest colour) and 5.64% fall under the alpha ramp and are fully transparent" "units: 1 scene unit = 1 mm in fsaverage space; x right, y superior, z posterior (anterior is -z); origin at the pial bounding-box centre (RAS x y z = .5 -17.8 15.4 mm)" "builder: build_brain_scene.py sha256 830c5ea341b38879 seed 20261106; mesh npz sha256 9f0f5d3c3667ac4d" "not a medical device; for demonstration and learning only"'/>
